\s1 The Vows of the Covenant
\b
\m 
\v 28 “The rest of the people—the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, temple servants,\f + \fr 10:28 \ft Hebrew Nethinim\f* and all who had separated themselves from the people of the land to obey the Law of God—along with their wives and all their sons and daughters who are able to understand, 
\v 29 hereby join with their noble brothers and commit themselves with a sworn oath to follow the Law of God given through His servant \zwd Moses|id="Q9077" t="2"\zwd* and to obey carefully all the commandments, ordinances, and statutes of the LORD our Lord. 
\b
\m 
\v 30 We will not give our daughters in marriage to the people of the land, and we will not take their daughters for our sons. 
\b
\m 
\v 31 When the people of the land bring merchandise or any kind of grain to sell on the Sabbath day, we will not buy from them on a Sabbath or holy day. Every seventh year we will let the fields lie fallow and will cancel every debt. 
\b
\m 
\v 32 We also place ourselves under the obligation to contribute a third of a shekel \f + \fr 10:32 \ft A third of a shekel is approximately 0.13 ounces or 3.8 grams, probably of silver.\f* yearly for the service of the house of our God: 
\v 33 for the showbread, for the regular grain offerings and burnt offerings, for the Sabbath offerings, for the New Moons and appointed feasts, for the holy offerings, for the sin offerings to make atonement for Israel, and for all the duties of the house of our God. 
\b
\m 
\v 34 We have cast lots among the priests, Levites, and people for the donation of wood by our families at the appointed times each year. They are to bring it to the house of our God to burn on the altar of the LORD our God, as it is written in the Law. 
\b
\m 
\v 35 We will also bring the firstfruits of our land and of every fruit tree to the house of the LORD year by year. 
\v 36 And we will bring the firstborn of our sons and our livestock, as it is written in the Law, and will bring the firstborn of our herds and flocks to the house of our God, to the priests who minister in the house of our God. 
\b
\m 
\v 37 Moreover, we will bring to the priests at the storerooms of the house of our God the firstfruits of our dough, of our grain offerings, of the fruit of all our trees, and of our new wine and oil. A tenth of our produce belongs to the Levites, so that they shall receive tithes in all the towns where we labor. 
\v 38 A priest of \zwd Aaron|id="Q51676" t="2"\zwd*’s line is to accompany the Levites when they collect the tenth, and the Levites are to bring a tenth of these tithes to the storerooms of the treasury in the house of our God. 
\v 39 For the Israelites and the Levites are to bring the contributions of grain, new wine, and oil to the storerooms where the articles of the sanctuary are kept and where the ministering priests, the gatekeepers, and the singers stay. 
\b
\m Thus we will not neglect the house of our God.” 
\c 11
\s1 Jerusalem’s New Settlers 
\m 
\v 1 Now the leaders of the people settled in Jerusalem, and the rest of the people cast lots to bring one out of ten to live in the holy city of Jerusalem, while the remaining nine \f + \fr 11:1 \ft Hebrew nine hands\f* were to dwell in their own towns. 
\v 2 And the people blessed all the men who volunteered to live in Jerusalem. 
\b
\m 
\v 3 These are the heads of the provinces who settled in Jerusalem. (In the villages of Judah, however, each lived on his own property in their towns—the Israelites, priests, Levites, temple servants,\f + \fr 11:3 \ft Hebrew Nethinim; also in verse 21\f* and descendants of \zwd Solomon|id="Q37085" t="2"\zwd*’s servants—
\v 4 while some of the descendants of \zwd Judah|id="Q282220" t="2"\zwd* and \zwd Benjamin|id="Q460763" t="2"\zwd* settled in Jerusalem.) 
\b
\m From the descendants of \zwd Judah|id="Q282220" t="2"\zwd*: 
\b
\pmo \zwd Athaiah son of \zwd Uzziah|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Zechariah|id="Q138772286" t="2"\zwd*, the son of \zwd Amariah|id="Q138721154" t="2"\zwd*, the son of \zwd Shephatiah|id="Q140030848" t="2"\zwd*, the son of \zwd Mahalalel|\zwd*, a descendant of \zwd Perez|id="Q1814684" t="2"\zwd*; 
\v 5 and \zwd Maaseiah son of \zwd Baruch|id="Q140047193" t="2"\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Col-hozeh|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Hazaiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Adaiah|id="Q138640478" t="2"\zwd*, the son of \zwd Joiarib|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Zechariah|id="Q138772321" t="2"\zwd*, a descendant of Shelah.\f + \fr 11:5 \ft Or of the Shilonite\f* 
\v 6 The descendants of \zwd Perez|id="Q1814684" t="2"\zwd* who settled in Jerusalem totaled 468 men of valor. 
\b
\m 
\v 7 From the descendants of \zwd Benjamin|Q460763\zwd*: 
\b
\pmo \zwd Sallu son of \zwd Meshullam|\zwd*|Q125747629\zwd*, the son of \zwd Joed|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Pedaiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Kolaiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Maaseiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Ithiel|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Jeshaiah|\zwd*; 
\v 8 and his followers \zwd Gabbai|\zwd* and \zwd Sallai|Q140472446\zwd*—928 men. 
\v 9 \zwd Joel son of \zwd Zichri|id="Q138792911" t="2"\zwd*|\zwd* was the officer over them, and \zwd Judah son of \zwd Hassenuah|\zwd*|\zwd* was over the Second District of the city.\f + \fr 11:9 \ft Or was over the Second Quarter of the city, a newer section of Jerusalem; or was second in command of the city\f* 
\b
\m 
\v 10 From the priests: 
\b
\li1 \zwd Jedaiah son of \zwd Joiarib|\zwd*|\zwd*;\f + \fr 11:10 \ft Or Jedaiah; the son of Joiarib;\f* \zwd Jachin|\zwd*; 
\v 11 \zwd Seraiah son of \zwd Hilkiah|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Meshullam|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Zadok|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Meraioth|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Ahitub|\zwd*, the chief official of the house of God; 
\v 12 and their associates who did the work at the temple—822 men; 
\b
\li1 \zwd Adaiah son of \zwd Jeroham|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Pelaliah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Amzi|id="Q138722307" t="2"\zwd*, the son of \zwd Zechariah|id="Q138772355" t="2"\zwd*, the son of \zwd Pashhur|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Malchijah|\zwd*; 
\v 13 and his associates, the leaders of families—242 men; 
\b
\li1 \zwd Amashai son of \zwd Azarel|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Ahzai|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Meshillemoth|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Immer|\zwd*; 
\v 14 and his associates \f + \fr 11:14 \ft Most LXX manuscripts; Hebrew their associates\f*—128 mighty men of valor. \zwd Zabdiel son of \zwd Haggedolim|\zwd*|Q138863473\zwd* was their overseer. 
\b
\m 
\v 15 From the Levites: 
\b
\pmo \zwd Shemaiah son of \zwd Hasshub|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Azrikam|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Hashabiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Bunni|\zwd*; 
\v 16 \zwd Shabbethai|Q140320763\zwd* and \zwd Jozabad|\zwd*, two leaders of the Levites, who supervised the work outside the house of God; 
\v 17 \zwd Mattaniah son of \zwd Mica|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Zabdi|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Asaph|\zwd*, who led in thanksgiving and prayer; \zwd Bakbukiah|Q139601236\zwd*, second among his associates; and \zwd Abda son of \zwd Shammua|\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Galal|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Jeduthun|\zwd*. 
\v 18 The Levites in the holy city totaled 284. 
\b
\m 
\v 19 And the gatekeepers: 
\b
\pmo \zwd Akkub|Q138713763\zwd*, \zwd Talmon|Q139678428\zwd*, and their associates, who kept watch at the gates—172 men. 
\s1 Residents Outside Jerusalem
\b
\m 
\v 20 The rest of the Israelites, with the priests and Levites, were in all the villages of Judah, each on his own inheritance. 
\v 21 The temple servants lived on the hill of Ophel, with \zwd Ziha|Q138834681\zwd* and \zwd Gishpa|\zwd* over them. 
\b
\m 
\v 22 Now the overseer of the Levites in Jerusalem was \zwd Uzzi son of \zwd Bani|\zwd*|Q139270863\zwd*, the son of \zwd Hashabiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Mattaniah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Mica|\zwd*.\f + \fr 11:22 \ft Mica is a variant of Micaiah; see Nehemiah 12:35.\f* He was one of \zwd Asaph|Q43280403\zwd*’s descendants, who were the singers in charge of the service of the house of God. 
\v 23 For there was a command from the king concerning the singers, an ordinance regulating their daily activities. 
\v 24 \zwd Pethahiah son of \zwd Meshezabel|\zwd*|\zwd*, a descendant of \zwd Zerah son of \zwd Judah|id="Q282220" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q3223065" t="2"\zwd*, was the king’s agent \f + \fr 11:24 \ft Hebrew hand\f* in every matter concerning the people. 
\b
\m 
\v 25 As for the villages with their fields, some of the people of Judah lived in Kiriath-arba, Dibon, Jekabzeel, and their villages; 
\v 26 in Jeshua, Moladah, and Beth-pelet; 
\v 27 in Hazar-shual; in Beersheba and its villages; 
\v 28 in Ziklag; in Meconah and its villages; 
\v 29 in En-rimmon, Zorah, Jarmuth, 
\v 30 Zanoah, Adullam, and their villages; in Lachish and its fields; and in Azekah and its villages. So they settled from Beersheba all the way to the Valley of Hinnom. 
\b
\m 
\v 31 The descendants of \zwd Benjamin|id="Q460763" t="2"\zwd* from Geba lived in Michmash, Aija, and Bethel with its villages; 
\v 32 in Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah, 
\v 33 Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim, 
\v 34 Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat, 
\v 35 Lod, and Ono; and in the Valley of the Craftsmen.\f + \fr 11:35 \ft Hebrew in Ge-harashim\f* 
\b
\m 
\v 36 And some divisions of the Levites of Judah settled in Benjamin. 
\c 12
\s1 The Priests and Levites Who Returned
\m 
\v 1 Now these are the priests and Levites who went up with \zwd Zerubbabel son of \zwd Shealtiel|id="Q2256348" t="2"\zwd*|Q320139\zwd* and with \zwd Jeshua|\zwd*: 
\b
\li1 \zwd Seraiah|\zwd*, \zwd Jeremiah|\zwd*, \zwd Ezra|Q191787\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 
\v 2 \zwd Amariah|\zwd*, \zwd Malluch|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:2 \ft Malluch is a variant of Malluchi; see verse 14.\f* \zwd Hattush|\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 
\v 3 \zwd Shecaniah|\zwd*, \zwd Rehum|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Rehum is a variant of Harim; see verse 15, Nehemiah 7:42, and Ezra 2:39.\f* \zwd Meremoth|\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 
\v 4 \zwd Iddo|\zwd*, \zwd Ginnethon|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:4 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts and Vulgate (see also verse 16); most MT manuscripts Ginnethoi\f* \zwd Abijah|\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 
\v 5 \zwd Mijamin|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:5 \ft Mijamin is a variant of Miniamin; see verse 17.\f* \zwd Maadiah|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:5 \ft Maadiah is a variant of Moadiah; see verse 17.\f* \zwd Bilgah|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:5 \ft Bilgah is a variant of Bilgai; also in verse 18; see Nehemiah 10:8.\f* 
\b
\li1 
\v 6 \zwd Shemaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Joiarib|\zwd*, \zwd Jedaiah|\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 
\v 7 \zwd Sallu|\zwd*, \zwd Amok|\zwd*, \zwd Hilkiah|\zwd*, and \zwd Jedaiah|\zwd*. 
\b
\li1 These were the leaders of the priests and their associates in the days of \zwd Jeshua|\zwd*. 
\b
\m 
\v 8 The Levites were \zwd Jeshua|\zwd*, \zwd Binnui|\zwd*, \zwd Kadmiel|\zwd*, \zwd Sherebiah|\zwd*, \zwd Judah|\zwd*, and \zwd Mattaniah|\zwd*, who, with his associates, led the songs of thanksgiving. 
\v 9 \zwd Bakbukiah|\zwd* and \zwd Unni|Q139490514\zwd*, their associates, stood across from them in the services. 
\b
\li1 
\v 10 \zwd Jeshua|Q783824\zwd* was the father of \zwd Joiakim|Q11979099\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 \zwd Joiakim|Q11979099\zwd* was the father of \zwd Eliashib|Q9252723\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 \zwd Eliashib|Q9252723\zwd* was the father of \zwd Joiada|Q6268944\zwd*, 
\b
\li1 
\v 11 \zwd Joiada|Q6268944\zwd* was the father of \zwd Jonathan|Q6215520\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:11 \ft Jonathan is a variant of Johanan; see verse 22.\f* 
\b
\li1 and \zwd Jonathan|Q6215520\zwd* was the father of \zwd Jaddua|Q2723012\zwd*. 
\b
\m 
\v 12 In the days of \zwd Joiakim|Q11979099\zwd*, these were the heads of the priestly families: 
\b
\li1 of the family of \zwd Seraiah|\zwd*, \zwd Meraiah|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Jeremiah|\zwd*, \zwd Hananiah|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 13 of \zwd Ezra|\zwd*, \zwd Meshullam|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Amariah|\zwd*, \zwd Jehohanan|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 14 of \zwd Malluchi|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:14 \ft Malluchi is a variant of Malluch; see verse 2.\f* \zwd Jonathan|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Shebaniah|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:14 \ft Shebaniah is a variant of Shecaniah; see verse 3; see also Syriac and some Hebrew and LXX manuscripts.\f* \zwd Joseph|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 15 of \zwd Harim|\zwd*, \zwd Adna|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Meraioth|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:15 \ft Meraioth is a variant of Meremoth; see verse 3 and also some LXX manuscripts.\f* \zwd Helkai|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 16 of \zwd Iddo|\zwd*, \zwd Zechariah|Q138772663\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Ginnethon|\zwd*, \zwd Meshullam|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 17 of \zwd Abijah|\zwd*, \zwd Zichri|Q138792923\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Miniamin|\zwd* and of \zwd Moadiah|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:17 \ft Moadiah is a variant of Maadiah; see verse 5.\f* \zwd Piltai|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 18 of \zwd Bilgah|\zwd*, \zwd Shammua|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Shemaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Jonathan|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 19 of \zwd Joiarib|\zwd*, \zwd Mattenai|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Jedaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Uzzi|Q139270899\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 20 of \zwd Sallai|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:20 \ft Sallai is a variant of Sallu; see verse 7.\f* \zwd Kallai|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 of \zwd Amok|Q138722243\zwd*, \zwd Eber|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 21 of \zwd Hilkiah|\zwd*, \zwd Hashabiah|\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 and of \zwd Jedaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Nethanel|\zwd*. 
\b
\m 
\v 22 In the days of \zwd Eliashib|Q9252723\zwd*, \zwd Joiada|Q6268944\zwd*, \zwd Johanan|Q6215520\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:22 \ft Johanan is a variant of Jonathan; see verse 11.\f* and \zwd Jaddua|Q2723012\zwd*, during the reign of \zwd Darius the Persian|\zwd*, the heads of the families of the Levites and priests were recorded. 
\b
\m 
\v 23 As for the descendants of \zwd Levi|id="Q215512" t="2"\zwd*, the family heads up to the days of \zwd Johanan son of \zwd Eliashib|id="Q9252723" t="2"\zwd*|Q6215520\zwd* were recorded in the Book of the Chronicles.\f + \fr 12:23 \ft Or the Book of the Annals or the Book of the Historical Events\f* 
\v 24 The leaders of the Levites were \zwd Hashabiah|\zwd*, \zwd Sherebiah|\zwd*, and \zwd Jeshua son of \zwd Kadmiel|\zwd*|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:24 \ft Or Sherebiah, Jeshua, Binnui, and Kadmiel\f* along with their associates, who stood across from them to give praise and thanksgiving as one section alternated with the other, as prescribed by \zwd David the man of God|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd*. 
\b
\m 
\v 25 \zwd Mattaniah|\zwd*, \zwd Bakbukiah|\zwd*, \zwd Obadiah|\zwd*, \zwd Meshullam|\zwd*, \zwd Talmon|Q139678428\zwd*, and \zwd Akkub|Q138713763\zwd* were gatekeepers who guarded the storerooms at the gates. 
\v 26 They served in the days of \zwd Joiakim son of \zwd Jeshua|id="Q783824" t="2"\zwd*|Q11979099\zwd*, the son of \zwd Jozadak|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:26 \ft Jozadak is a variant of Jehozadak; see 1 Chronicles 6:14.\f* and in the days of \zwd Nehemiah the governor|Q1025598\zwd* and \zwd Ezra the priest and scribe|Q191787\zwd*. 
\s1 The Dedication of the Wall
\b
\m 
\v 27 At the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, the Levites were sought out from all their homes and brought to Jerusalem to celebrate the joyous dedication with thanksgiving and singing, accompanied by cymbals, harps, and lyres. 
\v 28 The singers were also assembled from the region around Jerusalem, from the villages of the Netophathites, 
\v 29 from Beth-gilgal, and from the fields of Geba and Azmaveth, for they had built villages for themselves around Jerusalem. 
\v 30 After the priests and Levites had purified themselves, they purified the people, the gates, and the wall. 
\b
\m 
\v 31 Then I brought the leaders of Judah up on the wall, and I appointed two great thanksgiving choirs. One was to proceed along the top of the wall \f + \fr 12:31 \ft Or alongside the wall; also in verse 38\f* to the right, toward the Dung Gate. 
\v 32 \zwd Hoshaiah|\zwd* and half the leaders of Judah followed, 
\v 33 along with \zwd Azariah|\zwd*, \zwd Ezra|Q191787\zwd*, \zwd Meshullam|\zwd*, 
\v 34 \zwd Judah|\zwd*, \zwd Benjamin|Q140316349\zwd*, \zwd Shemaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Jeremiah|\zwd*, 
\v 35 and some of the priests with trumpets, and also \zwd Zechariah son of \zwd Jonathan|\zwd*|Q138772765\zwd*, the son of \zwd Shemaiah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Mattaniah|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Micaiah|\zwd*,\f + \fr 12:35 \ft Micaiah is a variant of Mica; see Nehemiah 11:22.\f* the son of \zwd Zaccur|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Asaph|\zwd*, 
\v 36 and his associates—\zwd Shemaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Azarel|Q139383649\zwd*, \zwd Milalai|\zwd*, \zwd Gilalai|\zwd*, \zwd Maai|\zwd*, \zwd Nethanel|\zwd*, \zwd Judah|\zwd*, and \zwd Hanani|\zwd*—with the musical instruments prescribed by \zwd David the man of God|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd*. \zwd Ezra the scribe|Q191787\zwd* led the procession. 
\v 37 At the Fountain Gate they went directly up the steps of the City of \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* on the ascent to the wall and passed above the house of \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* to the Water Gate on the east. 
\b
\m 
\v 38 The second thanksgiving choir proceeded to the left, and I followed it with half the people along the top of the wall, past the Tower of the Ovens to the Broad Wall, 
\v 39 over the Gate of Ephraim, the Jeshanah Gate,\f + \fr 12:39 \ft Or the Old City Gate\f* the Fish Gate, the Tower of \zwd Hananel|id="Q135646994" t="2"\zwd*, and the Tower of the Hundred, as far as the Sheep Gate. And they stopped at the Gate of the Guard. 
\b
\m 
\v 40 The two thanksgiving choirs then stood in the house of God, as did I, along with the half of the officials accompanying me, 
\v 41 as well as the priests with their trumpets—\zwd Eliakim|\zwd*, \zwd Maaseiah|\zwd*, \zwd Miniamin|\zwd*, \zwd Micaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Elioenai|\zwd*, \zwd Zechariah|Q138772765\zwd*, and \zwd Hananiah|\zwd*—
\v 42 and also \zwd Maaseiah|\zwd*, \zwd Shemaiah|\zwd*, \zwd Eleazar|\zwd*, \zwd Uzzi|\zwd*, \zwd Jehohanan|\zwd*, \zwd Malchijah|\zwd*, \zwd Elam|\zwd*, and \zwd Ezer|\zwd*. Then the choirs sang out under the direction of \zwd Jezrahiah|\zwd*. 
\b
\m 
\v 43 On that day they offered great sacrifices, rejoicing because God had given them great joy. The women and children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard from afar. 
\s1 Provisions for Temple Worship
\b
\m 
\v 44 And on that same day men were appointed over the rooms that housed the supplies, contributions, firstfruits, and tithes. The portions specified by the Law for the priests and Levites were gathered into these storerooms from the fields of the villages, because Judah rejoiced over the priests and Levites who were serving. 
\b
\m 
\v 45 They performed the service of their God and the service of purification, along with the singers and gatekeepers, as \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* and \zwd his son Solomon|id="Q37085" t="2"\zwd* had prescribed. 
\v 46 For long ago, in the days of \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* and \zwd Asaph|id="Q43280403" t="2"\zwd*, there were directors for the singers and for the songs of praise and thanksgiving to God. 
\b
\m 
\v 47 So in the days of \zwd Zerubbabel|Q320139\zwd* and \zwd Nehemiah|Q1025598\zwd*, all Israel contributed the daily portions for the singers and gatekeepers. They also set aside daily portions for the Levites, and the Levites set aside daily portions for the descendants of \zwd Aaron|id="Q51676" t="2"\zwd*. 
\c 13
\s1 Foreigners Excluded
\m 
\v 1 At that time the Book of \zwd Moses|id="Q9077" t="2"\zwd* was read aloud in the hearing of the people, and in it they found the passage stating that no Ammonite or Moabite should ever enter the assembly of God,\f + \fr 13:1 \ft See Deuteronomy 23:3–6.\f* 
\v 2 because they had not met the Israelites with food and water, but had hired \zwd Balaam|id="Q574641" t="2"\zwd* to call down a curse against them (although our God had turned the curse into a blessing). 
\b
\m 
\v 3 As soon as the people heard this law, they excluded from Israel all of foreign descent. 
\s1 The Temple Cleansed
\b
\m 
\v 4 Now before this, \zwd Eliashib the priest|Q9252723\zwd*, a relative of \zwd Tobiah|\zwd*, had been put in charge of the storerooms of the house of our God 
\v 5 and had prepared for \zwd Tobiah|\zwd* a large room where they had previously stored the grain offerings, the frankincense, the temple articles, and the tithes of grain, new wine, and oil prescribed for the Levites, singers, and gatekeepers, along with the contributions for the priests. 
\b
\m 
\v 6 \zdate|Q189689:P39:Q3114558:P580+P31Y\*While all this was happening, I was not in Jerusalem, because I had returned to \zwd Artaxerxes king of Babylon|Q189689\zwd* \f + \fr 13:6 \ft Artaxerxes king of Persia is identified here as the king of Babylon because Persia had conquered the Babylonian Empire.\f* in the thirty-second year of his reign. Some time later I obtained leave from \zwd the king|Q189689\zwd* 
\v 7 to return to Jerusalem. Then I discovered the evil that \zwd Eliashib|Q9252723\zwd* had done on behalf of \zwd Tobiah|\zwd* by providing him a room in the courts of the house of God. 
\b
\m 
\v 8 And I was greatly displeased and threw all of \zwd Tobiah|\zwd*’s household goods out of the room. 
\v 9 Then I ordered that the rooms be purified, and I had the articles of the house of God restored to them, along with the grain offerings and frankincense. 
\s1 Tithes Restored
\r (Leviticus 27:30–34; Deuteronomy 14:22–29; Deuteronomy 26:1–15)
\b
\m 
\v 10 I also learned that because the portions for the Levites had not been given to them, all the Levites and singers responsible for performing the service had gone back to their own fields. 
\v 11 So I rebuked the officials and asked, “Why has the house of God been neglected?” 
\b
\m Then I gathered the Levites and singers together and stationed them at their posts, 
\v 12 and all Judah brought a tenth of the grain, new wine, and oil into the storerooms. 
\v 13 I appointed as treasurers over the storerooms \zwd Shelemiah the priest|Q140131608\zwd*, \zwd Zadok the scribe|Q138862884\zwd*, and \zwd Pedaiah of the Levites|\zwd*, with \zwd Hanan son of \zwd Zaccur|id="Q138863241" t="2"\zwd*|\zwd*, the son of \zwd Mattaniah|\zwd*, to assist them, because they were considered trustworthy. They were responsible for distributing the supplies to their fellow Levites. 
\b
\m 
\v 14 Remember me for this, O my God, and do not blot out my deeds of loving devotion for the house of my God and for its services. 
\s1 The Sabbath Restored
\r (Jeremiah 17:19–27)
\b
\m 
\v 15 In those days I saw people in Judah treading winepresses on the Sabbath and bringing in grain and loading it on donkeys, along with wine, grapes, and figs. All kinds of goods were being brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day. So I warned them against selling food on that day. 
\v 16 Additionally, men of Tyre who lived there were importing fish and all kinds of merchandise and selling them on the Sabbath to the people of Judah in Jerusalem. 
\b
\m 
\v 17 Then I rebuked the nobles of Judah and asked, “What is this evil you are doing—profaning the Sabbath day? 
\v 18 Did not your forefathers do the same things, so that our God brought all this disaster on us and on this city? And now you are rekindling His wrath against Israel by profaning the Sabbath!” 
\b
\m 
\v 19 When the evening shadows began to fall on the gates of Jerusalem, just before the Sabbath, I ordered that the gates be shut and not opened until after the Sabbath. I posted some of my servants at the gates so that no load could enter on the Sabbath day. 
\b
\m 
\v 20 Once or twice, the merchants and those who sell all kinds of goods camped outside Jerusalem, 
\v 21 but I warned them, “Why are you camping in front of the wall? If you do it again, I will lay hands on you.” From that time on, they did not return on the Sabbath. 
\v 22 Then I instructed the Levites to purify themselves and guard the gates in order to keep the Sabbath day holy. 
\b
\m Remember me for this as well, O my God, and show me mercy according to Your abundant loving devotion. 
\s1 Intermarriage Forbidden
\r (Ezra 9:1–4)
\b
\m 
\v 23 In those days I also saw Jews who had married women from Ashdod, Ammon, and Moab. 
\v 24 Half of their children spoke the language of Ashdod or of the other peoples, but could not speak the language of Judah. 
\v 25 I rebuked them and called down curses on them. I beat some of these men and pulled out their hair. 
\b
\m Then I made them take an oath before God and said, “You must not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters as wives for your sons or for yourselves! 
\v 26 Did not \zwd King Solomon of Israel|id="Q37085" t="2"\zwd* sin in matters like this? There was not a king like him among many nations, and he was loved by his God, who made him king over all Israel—yet foreign women drew him into sin. 
\v 27 Must we now hear that you too are doing all this terrible evil and acting unfaithfully against our God by marrying foreign women?” 
\b
\m 
\v 28 Even one of the sons of \zwd Jehoiada son of \zwd Eliashib the high priest|id="Q9252723" t="2"\zwd*|Q6268944\zwd* had become a son-in-law to \zwd Sanballat the Horonite|Q751918\zwd*. Therefore I drove him away from me. 
\b
\m 
\v 29 Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood and the covenant of the priesthood and of the Levites. 
\b
\m 
\v 30 Thus I purified the priests and Levites from everything foreign, and I assigned specific duties to each of the priests and Levites. 
\v 31 I also arranged for contributions of wood at the appointed times, and for the firstfruits. 
\b
\m Remember me, O my God, with favor. 
